  "text": {
    "value": "The \"KeePassJava2\" project is an open-source Java library for working with KeePass password databases. It provides a headless (non-GUI) Java 8+ API to read and write KeePass 2.x database files (KDBX formats v3 and v4) and also reads the older 1.x version. It's designed for integration into your own Java or Android applications rather than being a standalone app.\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Read and write KeePass 2.x format (KDBX, versions 3 and 4)\n- Read KeePass 1.x format (Rijndael only)\n- Compatible with KeePass password safe for Windows, with no need for JCE policy files\n- Interfaces for Database, Group, and Entry objects for flexible integration\n- Licensed under Apache 2.0\n\n**Repository:**  \nYou can find the official repository here:  \nhttps://github.com/jorabin/KeePassJava2\n\n**Usage Example:**\n- Credentials and input stream are used to load a KeePass file, e.g.:\n  ```java\n  KdbxCreds creds = new KdbxCreds(\"password\".getBytes());\n  InputStream fileStream = ...;\n  Database database = SimpleDatabase.load(creds, fileStream);\n  ```\n- The library offers several implementations for database loading (Simple, JAXB, DOM), and you can traverse databases, groups, and entries programmatically.\n\n**Current status:**  \nThe latest main release is 2.2.4 (Java 8+). It’s regularly maintained and available through Maven Central using the coordinates:  \n```xml\n\u003cdependency\u003e\n  \u003cgroupId\u003eorg.linguafranca.pwdb\u003c/groupId\u003e\n  \u003cartifactId\u003eKeePassJava2\u003c/artifactId\u003e\n  \u003cversion\u003e2.2.4\u003c/version\u003e\n\u003c/dependency\u003e\n```\n\n**Documentation and more details** are available on the project's [GitHub page](https://github.com/jorabin/KeePassJava2)【3:0†source】【3:2†source】.",
